# Bot1 has Blood of the Martyr take the damage its own Nafs Asp deals to Bot2's blocking Ornithopter: the Asp has dealt
# damage to a player, its controller, and its ability triggers (the 2004-10-04 ruling). The loss waits for Bot1's next draw
# step, not the next draw step, Bot2's: Bot1 has lost nothing after it, and may still pay {1} in Bot2's end step, before
# their own draw step (CR 116.2c, 500.4). Having paid, they lose nothing at it.
[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Emerald
Mox Pearl
Nafs Asp
Blood of the Martyr
Plains x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Nafs Asp.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Hand.Blood of the Martyr.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Nafs Asp)
Bot2.Block(Ornithopter > Nafs Asp)
Bot1.Accept
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Life = 19
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Damage = 0
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot1.Life = 19
[T4 Bot2.End]
Bot1.Nafs Asp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
? Bot1.Mana =
[T5 Bot1.Main1]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 19
Bot2.Life = 20
